From 5bccd3a5d351464dc0ab50e8f1b5c2a858eaccc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:14:32 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 342/371] family server: the Black Pearl barricade forts stay
 in the island's ship-deployer zone instead of being moved onto the grid

0424 generates each fort in island zone 101 (PiratesGlobals.IslandShipDeployerZone), which every client near the
island watches. But DistributedFortAI is a DistributedMovingObjectAI (through DistributedBattleAvatarAI), and
DistributedIslandAI.handleChildArrive puts every moving-object child on the island grid, which moved the fort out of
101 by its position (centre cell 710 at generate, then 115 once the update task saw its real spot). No client had
interest there, so the forts stayed invisible and stage three of the Black Pearl still could not be played (boats'
BPFORT4).

handleChildArrive now leaves a child that arrives in IslandShipDeployerZone off the grid. Only the island's own
ShipDeployer (not a moving object) and the Black Pearl forts are generated in that zone; everything arriving in a
grid cell is unchanged. boats' sim_fortarrive.py (the real handleChildArrive, the real grid code, a real
DistributedFortAI subclass): HEAD FAIL (fort moves 710, 115, ends in 115), patched PASS (stays in 101, off the grid;
a moving object arriving in cell 710 is still put on the grid). AI only. The fort cannons (_createFortCannon) are
still made in grid cells; not changed here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 pirates/world/DistributedIslandAI.py | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pirates/world/DistributedIslandAI.py b/pirates/world/DistributedIslandAI.py
index d4944d4..2590173 100644
--- a/pirates/world/DistributedIslandAI.py
+++ b/pirates/world/DistributedIslandAI.py
@@ -48,7 +48,10 @@ class DistributedIslandAI(DistributedCartesianGridAI, DistributedGameAreaAI, Tea
         self.removeObjectFromGrid(av)
 
     def handleChildArrive(self, childObj, zoneId):
-        if isinstance(childObj, DistributedMovingObjectAI):
+        # A child generated in the ship-deployer zone stays there: the Black Pearl barricade
+        # forts are moving objects, and the grid moved them from zone 101 into the grid cell
+        # at their own spot, where no client 1000 ft out in the bay ever saw them (boats' BPFORT4).
+        if isinstance(childObj, DistributedMovingObjectAI) and zoneId != PiratesGlobals.IslandShipDeployerZone:
             self.addObjectToIslandGrid(childObj)
 
         # through DistributedGameAreaAI (it ends in DistributedNodeAI, the same call as
